<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 18 February, from 3102 BCE to 1943.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hinduism.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">3102 BCE <span class="tih-ago">5,127 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Kali Yuga begins, according to Hindu tradition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">According to Puranic sources, the day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> left the earth ended the Dvapara Yuga and began the Kali Yuga, the fourth and final yuga. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> astronomers placed its start at midnight between 17 and 18 February 3102 BCE.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1229">1229 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">797 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick II regains Jerusalem by treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixth-crusade">Sixth Crusade</a>, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> agreed a ten-year truce with the Ayyubid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a> that returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> to Christian control without a battle. The deal angered many on both sides.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1268">1268 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">758 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Novgorod and Pskov fight the Livonian Order at Wesenberg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rakvere">Rakvere</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, an army of Novgorod and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pskov">Pskov</a> under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-of-pereslavl">Dmitry of Pereslavl</a> fought the forces of Danish Estonia and the Livonian Order. Both sides claimed victory, but the crusaders' advance against Novgorod was checked.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wesenberg-1268">Battle of Wesenberg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-crusades">Northern Crusades</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1564">1564 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">462 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Michelangelo dies in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The sculptor, painter and architect died aged 88, still working as chief architect of St Peter's. His works include the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistine-chapel">Sistine Chapel</a> ceiling and the Last Judgement.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1678">1678 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">348 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Bunyan's 'The Pilgrim's Progress' is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Partly written in Bedford gaol, Bunyan's allegory of Christian's journey to the Celestial City was an immediate success. It has been translated into more than 200 languages.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1885">1885 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">141 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mark Twain's 'Adventures of Huckleberry Finn' published in the US</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Twain's novel of a boy and an escaped slave on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> was published in America. Written in vernacular speech, it has been called the source of all modern American literature.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1930">1930 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">96 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Clyde Tombaugh discovers Pluto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Comparing photographic plates at Lowell Observatory, Tombaugh found a faint moving object. Named Pluto at the suggestion of 11-year-old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> Burney, it was reclassified as a dwarf planet in 2006.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hans and Sophie Scholl arrested in Munich</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The siblings of the White Rose resistance group were caught distributing anti-Nazi leaflets at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> University. They were tried and guillotined four days later.</p></div></li></ol>
